      "rationale": "📖️ A READER, and that is the whole point of registering it separately.\n\nThis subset also carries a `🦀️.rs` that COMPUTES what each mutation should produce. That entry is registered `cross-semio-implementation` and does not discharge anything, because both halves of such a comparison descend from one reading of the specification.\n\nThis entry is a different mechanism. The expected state is not computed at all — it is COMMITTED, as the `after` half of a byte-reproducible fixture. `jszip` 3.10.1 then parses the BCF 2.1 zip container on BOTH sides and the comparison is over what it recovered. The probes say so in their own header: \"Everything here MARSHALS and READS; nothing here applies a mutation or predicts what one should.\"\n\nSo the judge is a third-party implementation of the format, and nothing in this repository predicts the answer it is judging. That is what makes it qualifying where the sibling entry is not.",
